            <ArticleTitle>Ultrafast Excited-State Dynamics of V_{3}O_{5} as a Signature of a Photoinduced Insulator-Metal Phase Transition.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>057602</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1103/PhysRevLett.119.057602</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The ultrafast elastic light scattering technique is applied to reveal the strong nonlinearity of V_{3}O_{5} associated with a photoinduced insulator-metal phase transition. Observation of time-domain relaxation dynamics suggests several stages of structural transition. We discuss the nonequilibrium processes in V_{3}O_{5} in terms of photoinduced melting of a polaronic Wigner crystal, coalescence of V-O octahedra, and photogeneration of acoustical phonons in the low-T and high-T phases of V_{3}O_{5}. A molecular dynamics computation supports experimentally observed stages of V_{3}O_{5} relaxation dynamics.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
